{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception as a single automaton, capturing the interaction between motion commands and obstacle sensor events. The specification automata encode safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacles. All transitions are deterministic and respect the runtime semantics and safety constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Plant G1 combines robot motion and perception into a single automaton, with states representing the robot's current perception and action context.",
    "Specifications E1-E4 bind each perception state to exactly one allowed controllable action, enforcing conservative recovery and maximizing exploration progress in clear states."
  ],
